Round 3 of branch codex/kernel-setup-fix (on top of b21e400). Dec 027 FIDELITY still applies: the timing kernel may only reproduce data/raw/docker/docker/Dockerfile.public (pip + the line-9 tool set), offline. NO PIP_NO_INDEX/PIP_RETRIES/PIP_TIMEOUT prefixes. setup_calls logging stays mandatory.

Problem (local acceptance run of eval/repro/plan003_kernel_setup.py, results/plan003_kernel_setup_acceptance.json, status failed): with SETUP_FIX=1, step tool_install (eval/kaggle/agent_timing.py install_tools(), ~line 293) fails for both tasks: "Could not find a version that satisfies the requirement pathspec>=0.10.1 (from hatchling)". The competition wheelhouse (data/raw/wheels) does not hold the full dependency closure of the line-9 tool set: pathspec and trove-classifiers (hatchling), shellingham (typer) are missing, as is pytest-timeout 2.1.0. Dockerfile.public line 9 installed the tools WITH their dependencies from PyPI at image build time, so the scorer image has them.

Fix:
1. Install the line-9 tools with `--no-deps` (still --no-index --find-links=/wheels, --ignore-installed). Then compute the runtime dependency closure of those tools (Requires-Dist from each chosen wheel's METADATA, evaluated with packaging markers for the SANDBOX interpreter from the interpreter_probe; skip extras). For each dependency not satisfied: prefer a compatible wheel from the wheelhouse (install --no-deps, offline); otherwise copy it from the running interpreter with the existing copy_runtime_package() (pure-Python only, as done for pip/pytest-timeout). Recurse until closed.
2. Log a new setup_calls step "tool_deps" with, per dependency: name, required spec, source (wheelhouse path | runtime copy | missing), version installed. If a dependency is missing everywhere, do NOT abort: record it in a per-task list "missing_tool_deps" and continue (the tool itself stays installed). Abort only when a TOP-LEVEL line-9 tool has no source (existing behaviour).
3. After installation, run `python3 -m pip check` in the sandbox as step "pip_check"; record rc and the bounded output. Non-fatal.
4. Keep everything else: bounded stdout/stderr (2 KB), task ids only, never task text, stage_kernel.py single-file staging, the starter docker_image pin (py3.12, cp312 wheelhouse), SETUP_FIX=0 path unchanged.
5. Tests (offline): unit tests for the closure computation (markers, extras skipped, wheelhouse preferred over runtime copy, missing recorded not fatal, cycle-safe) using tiny synthetic wheels in tmp_path. Full eval/tests must stay green.
Acceptance: the Builder will re-run eval/repro/plan003_kernel_setup.py locally (bwrap may be blocked in your sandbox; say so if it is). Target: both modes status ok, editable_rc 0 in both modes for rich_3006 and fastapi_14986, tool_install rc 0, tool_deps + pip_check present.
